WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.889
Chapter ten: frequently asked questions and known limitations.

00:00:03.889 --> 00:00:06.460
First, short answers to common questions.

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:10.875
Then the deliberate limits of this release, and one known issue.

00:00:10.875 --> 00:00:15.563
Is Scholium free? Yes. Scholium is free to read and free to publish.

00:00:15.563 --> 00:00:20.001
Is Scholium a journal? No. Scholium lists, reviews and badges papers.

00:00:20.001 --> 00:00:25.468
Listing means that a moderator found the submission in scope and within the policies.

00:00:25.468 --> 00:00:28.763
It does not mean that the science is correct.

00:00:28.763 --> 00:00:31.457
The formal reviews are where the work is judged.

00:00:31.457 --> 00:00:33.877
They show openly, next to the paper.

00:00:33.877 --> 00:00:38.243
Can I post a paper that is also on arXiv, or submit it to a journal?

00:00:38.243 --> 00:00:43.187
Cross-posting is expected. Choose a licence that your target journal accepts.

00:00:43.187 --> 00:00:47.760
The licence picker tells you which licences most journals accept.

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:50.445
Can I change my paper after it is published?

00:00:50.445 --> 00:00:54.228
Not the version itself, because a signed version is permanent.

00:00:54.228 --> 00:00:59.509
Publish a new version with a change note. Every earlier version stays available.

00:00:59.509 --> 00:01:03.496
Can I delete my paper? No. Scholium keeps a permanent record.

00:01:03.496 --> 00:01:08.921
You can issue a withdrawal or a retraction notice, which shows alongside the paper.

00:01:08.921 --> 00:01:16.315
A moderator takes down content that must be removed for legal reasons, and a notice of its removal remains.

00:01:16.315 --> 00:01:18.766
Why does every paper say anchor pending?

00:01:18.766 --> 00:01:22.505
Public blockchain timestamps are planned for a later release.

00:01:22.505 --> 00:01:26.428
Your browser still checks signatures, history and files in full.

00:01:26.428 --> 00:01:31.669
Signed, anchor pending is the best result in this release. It is not a warning.

00:01:31.669 --> 00:01:35.035
My badge says could not check. Is the paper fake? No.

00:01:35.035 --> 00:01:41.069
Your browser could not finish the check, usually because you are offline or the server is busy.

00:01:41.069 --> 00:01:43.120
Choose Re-run check later.

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:48.256
Only Verification failed, with a red cross, means that something does not match.

00:01:48.256 --> 00:01:50.990
Who can see my email address? Nobody else.

00:01:50.990 --> 00:01:55.156
Scholium uses it to confirm your account and to send you emails.

00:01:55.156 --> 00:01:57.174
It never shows on your profile.

00:01:57.174 --> 00:02:02.651
Your name, affiliation and email are stored encrypted, and you can erase them.

00:02:02.651 --> 00:02:05.354
Will authors know who reviewed their paper?

00:02:05.354 --> 00:02:08.622
Not if you review anonymously, which is the default.

00:02:08.622 --> 00:02:10.760
Your review appears as Reviewer A.

00:02:10.760 --> 00:02:14.805
Your identity is held in escrow for misconduct cases only.

00:02:14.805 --> 00:02:19.685
If you choose Sign with my name instead, your review shows on your public profile.

00:02:19.685 --> 00:02:22.421
Why can't I see the reviews on a paper yet?

00:02:22.421 --> 00:02:27.191
Reviews stay sealed until a second reviewer commits, or until 21 days pass.

00:02:27.191 --> 00:02:29.990
Then each reviewer reveals their own review.

00:02:29.990 --> 00:02:33.952
The Reviews tab tells you when a report is still sealed.

00:02:33.952 --> 00:02:37.819
Does the AI pre-review affect the status of my paper? No.

00:02:37.819 --> 00:02:42.364
It is advisory only, and there is no path from AI output to status.

00:02:42.364 --> 00:02:44.528
You can rebut any finding.

00:02:44.528 --> 00:02:47.308
I lost my phone or laptop. What do I do?

00:02:47.308 --> 00:02:52.728
On a new device, go to the recover page and start recovery with your ORCID iD.

00:02:52.728 --> 00:02:58.688
Three of your five guardians must approve. Then a 72-hour safety window follows.

00:02:58.688 --> 00:03:03.527
Without a linked ORCID iD and saved guardians, recovery is not possible.

00:03:03.527 --> 00:03:05.339
So set up both early.

00:03:05.339 --> 00:03:07.838
How do I become a reviewer or moderator?

00:03:07.838 --> 00:03:12.800
The node operator grants tiers three and four. Contact the node operator.

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:14.299
What emails will I get?

00:03:14.299 --> 00:03:18.795
Email confirmation, co-author consent requests, and the daily digest.

00:03:18.795 --> 00:03:25.189
Also the notice that someone started a recovery of your account, if your email is confirmed.

00:03:25.189 --> 00:03:30.294
Everything else is a notification in Scholium, in the bell or on your dashboard.

00:03:30.294 --> 00:03:39.499
This includes moderation outcomes, report outcomes, appeal notices, and the recovery requests that you are asked to approve as a guardian.

00:03:39.499 --> 00:03:43.840
Now the known limitations. These are deliberate limits of the first release.

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:45.211
Plan around them.

00:03:45.211 --> 00:03:49.680
Accounts. One browser holds one account. You cannot add a second device.

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:54.549
If you sign in from another browser, you create a new, separate account.

00:03:54.549 --> 00:03:57.982
You can edit your profile only on the onboarding page.

00:03:57.982 --> 00:04:01.115
You cannot unlink or re-link your ORCID iD.

00:04:01.115 --> 00:04:04.385
Publishing. You must add co-authors by their DID.

00:04:04.385 --> 00:04:07.656
Lookup by ORCID iD or email is not available yet.

00:04:07.656 --> 00:04:12.928
Your browser keeps your submission drafts. The server does not keep them.

00:04:12.928 --> 00:04:17.090
Scholium does not read the abstract from your file, so paste it in.

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:21.094
Claiming a paper imported from arXiv is not available yet.

00:04:21.094 --> 00:04:25.834
Reviewing. You cannot save a review draft, so complete the form in one sitting.

00:04:25.834 --> 00:04:30.795
Revealing is manual. Come back and choose Reveal review when the gate opens.

00:04:30.795 --> 00:04:34.080
Your review key lives in the browser where you committed.

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:37.766
If you might switch browsers, export the review key file.

00:04:37.766 --> 00:04:40.366
You cannot accept or decline invitations.

00:04:40.366 --> 00:04:45.334
Scholium records review ratings, but does not use them for anything yet.

00:04:45.334 --> 00:04:50.320
Discussion. You cannot edit or delete posts, and you cannot withdraw helpful votes.

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:53.904
There is no blocking, and no muting from the web app.

00:04:53.904 --> 00:04:58.955
Annotations attach to a whole paragraph. They do not carry over to new versions.

00:04:58.955 --> 00:04:59.491
Network.

00:04:59.491 --> 00:05:05.518
Public timestamps, called anchoring, are not enabled, so every paper shows anchor pending.

00:05:05.518 --> 00:05:08.665
Each server keeps one local copy of each paper.

00:05:08.665 --> 00:05:12.347
Replication across several operators comes later.

00:05:12.347 --> 00:05:17.564
One known issue. A recovery of your own account also shows as a guardian request.

00:05:17.564 --> 00:05:22.923
It shows on your dashboard, and under Recovery requests on the security page.

00:05:22.923 --> 00:05:24.052
Do not approve it.

00:05:24.052 --> 00:05:29.531
Cancel it, as chapter two describes in the section: a recovery you did not start.

00:05:29.531 --> 00:05:32.882
In short: Scholium is free, and it is not a journal.

00:05:32.882 --> 00:05:37.199
A signed version is permanent, and anchor pending is not a warning.

00:05:37.199 --> 00:05:42.560
Plan around the limits of this first release. Next, chapter eleven: glossary.
